WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:21.836
Jason walked into the gym and bumped into a tall, young woman. "Ooph!"

2
00:00:21.837 --> 00:00:25.327
"Jason, I'd like you to meet Allison.

3
00:00:25.328 --> 00:00:29.251
She's from Penny's Dog Shelter," said Mr. Dunn.

4
00:00:29.252 --> 00:00:33.137
"Penny's Dog Shelter?" Jason was excited.

5
00:00:33.138 --> 00:00:36.117
"My mom and I like to visit the dogs there.

6
00:00:36.118 --> 00:00:39.501
My favorite one is Lucy.

7
00:00:39.502 --> 00:00:41.814
But we can't adopt her.

8
00:00:41.815 --> 00:00:44.459
My dad is allergic."

9
00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:51.640
Allison smiled. "I'm sure Lucy enjoys your visits."

10
00:00:51.641 --> 00:00:54.641
"And guess what!" cried Izzie.

11
00:00:54.642 --> 00:00:58.024
"We're going to visit the shelter tomorrow!"

12
00:00:58.025 --> 00:01:00.568
"Yeah," added Ethan.

13
00:01:00.569 --> 00:01:04.031
"Allison is going to show us how to make dog treats.

14
00:01:04.032 --> 00:01:06.837
We can bring them to the dogs tomorrow."

15
00:01:06.838 --> 00:01:10.762
"We're making peanut butter treats," said Allison.

16
00:01:10.763 --> 00:01:13.860
"Because almost all dogs love peanut butter.

17
00:01:13.861 --> 00:01:16.417
These treats are really easy to make.

18
00:01:16.418 --> 00:01:19.034
They only have four ingredients!"

19
00:01:19.035 --> 00:01:24.537
"Peanut butter and . . . ?" Izzie began to guess.

20
00:01:24.538 --> 00:01:29.470
"And water, whole wheat flour, and oats," said Allison.

21
00:01:29.471 --> 00:01:33.994
"Can you preheat the oven to 175 degrees, Mr. Dunn?"

22
00:01:33.995 --> 00:01:38.226
"Yes," said Mr. Dunn.

23
00:01:38.227 --> 00:01:42.998
"First we mix the dry ingredients in a large bowl," said Allison.

24
00:01:42.999 --> 00:01:46.583
"We need two cups of flour and one cup of oats."

25
00:01:46.584 --> 00:01:54.901
Ethan and Bobby measured the dry ingredients.

26
00:01:54.902 --> 00:01:59.138
"Now we have to spray the measuring cup with oil," Allison said.

27
00:01:59.139 --> 00:02:02.319
"So the peanut butter will come out more easily!"

28
00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:05.300
Mr. Dunn knew what to do next.

29
00:02:05.301 --> 00:02:15.191
"Nina, can you please get one and a quarter cups of hot water?"

30
00:02:15.192 --> 00:02:19.172
Jason dumped the peanut butter into a bowl.

31
00:02:19.173 --> 00:02:28.473
Then Nina added the hot water while Jason stirred.

32
00:02:28.474 --> 00:02:34.265
"Now let's add the peanut butter mix to the dry mix," said Allison.

33
00:02:34.266 --> 00:02:37.842
"Combine until it becomes a nice dough ball."

34
00:02:37.843 --> 00:02:40.795
Izzie started kneading the mixture.

35
00:02:40.796 --> 00:02:44.140
Next Allison held up a rolling pin.

36
00:02:44.141 --> 00:02:46.810
"Now we're ready for the fun part!

37
00:02:46.811 --> 00:02:50.684
Jason, please sprinkle some flour on the table."

38
00:02:50.685 --> 00:02:57.363
Jason did, and then Izzie dropped the dough ball on it.

39
00:02:57.364 --> 00:03:06.650
"Nina, please roll out the dough until it's about six millimeters thick," Allison said.

40
00:03:06.651 --> 00:03:12.292
"I love using rolling pins!" Nina said, rolling happily.

41
00:03:12.293 --> 00:03:20.309
Bobby laughed. "You look like a pizza maker, Nina!" he said.

42
00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:24.426
Allison picked up a cookie cutter shaped like a dog bone.

43
00:03:24.427 --> 00:03:28.537
"Everyone, grab a cookie cutter and start cutting out bones!

44
00:03:28.538 --> 00:03:31.085
Press the cutter into the dough.

45
00:03:31.086 --> 00:03:34.912
Wiggle it around and then lift it up.

46
00:03:34.913 --> 00:03:42.963
Then place the bone-shaped dough on the cookie tray."

47
00:03:42.964 --> 00:03:46.746
Jason lined up his dog-bone treats on the tray.

48
00:03:46.747 --> 00:03:52.004
He hoped Lucy liked peanut butter and that no one adopted her before tomorrow!

49
00:03:52.005 --> 00:03:55.599
He couldn't wait to give her a special treat.

50
00:03:55.600 --> 00:04:02.497
"Bake the treats for forty minutes," Allison told the campers.

51
00:04:02.498 --> 00:04:05.149
"I have to go back to the shelter now.

52
00:04:05.150 --> 00:04:07.369
But I'll see you tomorrow.

53
00:04:07.370 --> 00:04:10.073
Don't forget to bring the treats!"

54
00:04:10.074 --> 00:04:13.957
"Bye, Allison! Thank you!"

55
00:04:13.958 --> 00:04:18.056
The campers waved good-bye.

56
00:04:18.057 --> 00:04:23.015
The next day the campers arrived at Penny's with dog bones.

57
00:04:23.016 --> 00:04:26.254
Jason looked down the row of cages.

58
00:04:26.255 --> 00:04:29.952
He spotted his favorite dog right away.

59
00:04:29.953 --> 00:04:32.548
"Lucy!" he cried.

60
00:04:32.549 --> 00:04:34.506
"Here's a peanut butter treat.

61
00:04:34.507 --> 00:04:43.071
Just for you!"
